  "problem": "Consider the following arithmetic sequence.\n\n$$\n-22,\\,-31,\\,-40,\\,-49,\\,…\n$$\n\nThe common difference of this arithmetic sequence is{{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "The common difference $d$ of an arithmetic sequence is the difference between any two consecutive terms.\n\nTherefore, the common difference for our sequence is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{2}-{a}_{1} \\\\  & =-31-(-22) \\\\  & =-31+22 \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
